4.4  Apple platform
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    SPARTA builds against the Metal, Foundation and Accelerate frameworks and
    uses `xcrun clang` at build time, all governed by the Apple SDK licence
    terms. Accelerate supplies BLAS and LAPACK to the CPU backend. Nothing
    Apple-owned is redistributed: the frameworks are linked dynamically from
    the end user's system, and `src/kernels/*.metal` are embedded as source
    text and compiled at runtime by the end user's own Metal driver.

4.5  BLAS and LAPACK on other platforms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Outside Apple, a build links the BLAS and LAPACK library named by the
    SPARTA_BLAS_LIB environment variable at build time, for example OpenBLAS
    (BSD-3-Clause) or Intel MKL (Intel Simplified Software License). Without
    it nothing is linked. Whoever redistributes such a build together with the
    library must ship that library's own licence and notices as well.


