5.1  Provenance of the symbolic phase
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Until September 2026 the symbolic analysis and the fill-reducing orderings were
copied from RSLAB, a fork of feral. All of it was replaced between 14 and
15 September 2026, because the upstream copyright position could not be
established. NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY DERIVES FROM RSLAB OR FERAL.

What replaced it, and what each was written from:

    src/symbolic/column_counts.rs
        Gilbert, Ng & Peyton, SIAM J. Matrix Anal. Appl. 15(4):1075-1091
        (1994). Detailed record in COL_COUNTS.md section 7, removed in
        a5985e4 (`git show a5985e4^:COL_COUNTS.md`).

    src/symbolic/elimination_tree.rs, postorder.rs
        George & Liu, Computer Solution of Large Sparse Positive Definite
        Systems (1981) ch. 5; Liu, SIAM J. Matrix Anal. Appl. 11(1):134-172
        (1990).

    src/symbolic/supernode.rs
        Fundamental supernodes per Liu, Ng & Peyton, ACM TOMS 19 (1993)
        302-325. Merge rule per SPRAL SSIDS, section 2.1.

    The fill-reducing ordering
        Replaced by METIS in September 2026, and METIS by SCALPEL
        (crates/scalpel, original SPARTA work) in October 2026.

    devtools/matgen/
        Written from the physics: the time-harmonic curl-curl Maxwell operator
        on a structured grid, discretised through curl curl = L - grad div.

No code was taken from any existing implementation of these algorithms. In
particular: no CSparse or CXSparse, no code listings from Davis's textbook, no
SuiteSparse, no SSIDS, no METIS source, and no RSLAB.

Verification. The replacements are behaviour-preserving, which is a stronger
check than passing tests: the plan digest -- a hash of everything the numeric
phase consumes, including the ordering and the full supernode partition -- is
unchanged on every test system, and nnz(L) is identical on all six curl-curl
sizes up to 113,335,262 nonzeros.

Limitations, which counsel should see rather than discover. This work was done
by a large language model under human direction. For column_counts.rs the prior
implementation had already been deleted and was never read, so that record is
a genuine clean room. For the other files the prior implementation WAS read
before being rewritten: the algorithms are published and unprotectable, the
expression differs throughout, and no other implementation was consulted, but
it is a reimplementation with knowledge of the original rather than a clean
room. Separately, an LLM's training corpus cannot be certified free of any
widely published code. The obligation these files ever carried was attribution,
not copyleft. Having an engineer read them against the cited papers and sign
off, dated, would convert this from "LLM-authored, documented" to
"human-reviewed and adopted"; roughly two hours for about 1,500 lines.
